'''

-Input means taking data from the user.
-Output means displaying data to the user.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
| Function  | Purpose                                      | Example                |
| --------- | -------------------------------------------- | ---------------------- |
| `input()` | Takes input from the user                    | `name = input()`       |
| `print()` | Displays output                              | `print(name)`          |
| `int()`   | Converts input to an integer                 | `int(input())`         |
| `float()` | Converts input to a decimal number           | `float(input())`       |
| `f""`     | Formats output with variables                | `print(f"Age: {age}")` |
| `sep`     | Changes the separator between printed values | `print(1, 2, sep="-")` |
| `end`     | Changes what is printed at the end           | `print("Hi", end=" ")` |
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- '''